    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493338438/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """<Hotel Webster, New York> Thursday, Jan. 7, 1909
Cold.
Hutchins came in to breakfast, and was as sincere and “elemental” as ever.
Bernhard lunched with Lamont (editor of  The Nation ), and I stayed in and worked upon my lecture.
Bernhard called on Mrs. Hewitt and met a very nice Mrs. Tiffany.
Grace came to see me, and Mr. John Van Dyke, and various other people.
We went to the Boston Symphony with the Spaldings to hear Alberto’s rival, Mischa Ehman, play. He is a horrid youngster, but plays, I think, better than dear Alberto. They gave an  awful  thing of Noren’s first ‚ a disgrace to the orchestra, but a piece of German advertising."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 17 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1909> .

